WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.030 --> 00:00:06.059
There are a lot of things in Bloodborne that I never really got to talk about. These are discoveries that shocked or impressed

00:00:06.339 --> 00:00:10.379
impressed me in some way when I learned about them, so when I tell you about them today,

00:00:10.380 --> 00:00:13.590
I'm kind of betting that you guys will give the same response.

00:00:13.809 --> 00:00:18.628
Let's get started: the first is something that blew people's minds about five months ago.

00:00:18.970 --> 00:00:25.560
User "chim cheree" [?] of Reddit didn't run past the Winter Lantern enemy like a sane person would.

00:00:25.900 --> 00:00:32.009
Instead, she actually took the time to look closely at it and study it. What she found was pretty chilling.

00:00:32.230 --> 00:00:37.890
She discovered that the Winter Lanterns bear striking resemblance to the Plain Doll from our dream,

00:00:38.079 --> 00:00:42.269
down to the smallest little detail on their clothing, every fold of the cloth, even.

00:00:42.460 --> 00:00:47.129
When you read over that thread now you realize that most people didn't believe her at first,

00:00:47.590 --> 00:00:51.629
until a guy named Jeremy took high-res screenshots of the enemy.

00:00:51.699 --> 00:00:53.699
Let's take a close look at what they found.

00:00:53.860 --> 00:00:57.460
The Red Scarf overlays perfectly with this piece of flesh,

00:00:57.460 --> 00:01:00.569
the four seams on the torso are visible on the Lantern's clothing,

00:01:00.640 --> 00:01:04.559
the corset even takes the same angle on both waists

00:01:04.559 --> 00:01:09.300
and there's even the rumpled V-shaped edge that runs around the entire body.

00:01:09.300 --> 00:01:11.970
The only thing that doesn't appear is the Doll's shawl,

00:01:12.100 --> 00:01:16.509
but even that could be represented by the tendrils coming down from the brain.

00:01:16.509 --> 00:01:18.600
So what are the consequences of this?

00:01:18.759 --> 00:01:23.140
What is the relationship between the Doll and the Winter Lanterns?

00:01:23.140 --> 00:01:26.600
With the knowledge we have I feel like there's only two explanations.

00:01:26.600 --> 00:01:28.679
My short answer, for this video,

00:01:28.680 --> 00:01:34.979
is that the doll in Mensis's Nightmare must appear there as a figment of our own consciousness.

00:01:35.140 --> 00:01:40.800
Or perhaps the doll imagery was brought into the nightmare by Micolash when the dream was conceived.

00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:46.079
There's a lot I want to say on this, but it's too detailed for this video, so I'll write a document

00:01:46.079 --> 00:01:49.660
and I'll leave a link to it in the description if you're interested.

00:01:49.660 --> 00:01:54.500
Moving on, but still speaking of the Doll, 
did you know that she has eyes on the inside of her head?

00:01:54.500 --> 00:01:57.149
Most of you probably learned this trick from EpicNameBro,

00:01:57.149 --> 00:02:01.300
who did it in his first episode of his Bloodborne Let's Play, I believe.

00:02:01.300 --> 00:02:07.559
Having eyes on the inside is synonymous with gaining Insight, as mentioned by the Third of the Umbilical Cord

00:02:07.840 --> 00:02:11.280
description and it makes you wonder: do you think her eyes here are

00:02:11.940 --> 00:02:17.700
a part of a badly mapped texture, are they a hidden Easter Egg or are they something more?

00:02:17.700 --> 00:02:20.610
Surely there's more to the Doll than there seems at first glance.

00:02:21.220 --> 00:02:27.300
She even has a unique piece of dialogue that you can easily go the whole game without hearing.

00:02:27.300 --> 00:02:33.300
The requirements for this dialogue appearing are pretty unclear, but it should eventually happen to you.

00:02:33.300 --> 00:02:33.960
Have a listen:

00:02:34.400 --> 00:02:38.519
"Oh Flora, of the moon, of the dream,

00:02:40.240 --> 00:02:44.700
Oh little ones, Oh fleeting will of the ancients,

00:02:46.030 --> 00:02:48.030
let the Hunter be safe,

00:02:48.670 --> 00:02:50.670
let him find comfort,

00:02:51.280 --> 00:02:55.619
and let this dream, his captor, foretell a pleasant awakening."

00:02:56.980 --> 00:03:01.739
The doll wants you to be safe. She wants you to awaken and to forget.

00:03:02.260 --> 00:03:06.100
Basically, she wants you to go through with the 'Accept Death' ending,

00:03:06.100 --> 00:03:12.000
where you kneel before Gherman, the ending that other hunters like Djura and Eileen surely got,

00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:16.769
hunters who experienced the dream, likely served a purpose on a different night of the hunt,

00:03:17.170 --> 00:03:21.449
and then were removed. When Gherman grants you mercy, you become one of the many

00:03:21.449 --> 00:03:25.800
gravestones marking the other Hunters who passed through here as you did.

00:03:25.800 --> 00:03:32.500
In New Game+, you will sometimes spawn in to see the Doll behind you, kneeling at your earlier grave.

00:03:32.500 --> 00:03:36.833
To me, it's a neat reference to what Bloodborne's New Game+ represents.

00:03:36.833 --> 00:03:40.800
It implies that the dream continues even after you pass through it.

00:03:41.440 --> 00:03:44.219
Somehow [the] dream must be useful to whatever

00:03:44.470 --> 00:03:50.399
maintains it, be it Gherman, the Moon Presence, or maybe even the Doll from what we've seen.

00:03:50.400 --> 00:03:54.500
And did you know that before you start your final fight with Gherman,

00:03:54.500 --> 00:03:57.030
that it's possible to PVP in the hunters dream?

00:03:57.250 --> 00:04:01.830
It's a pretty fantastic setting, although this isn't easy to do. Your Sinister Resonant

00:04:01.830 --> 00:04:07.469
Bell is grayed out, so the only way to PVP is to summon help for you in your boss fight

00:04:07.470 --> 00:04:13.169
and then kill them. The adversary system is one of those really hidden mechanics in Blood-Borne.

00:04:13.360 --> 00:04:19.679
It relates to the fourth rune you have memorized, so it basically makes it so that Vilebloods can fight

00:04:20.080 --> 00:04:26.120
Executioners, vice versa, and also so that Hunters of Hunters can kill blood-addled Hunters.

00:04:26.120 --> 00:04:30.479
For example, if you're a Vileblood with the Corruption Rune equipped and you back in a

00:04:30.479 --> 00:04:34.019
Executioner with the Radiance Rune equipped, he won't be friendly.

00:04:34.020 --> 00:04:35.560
He'll be your adversary.

00:04:35.560 --> 00:04:41.970
These enemies appear purple in your world, a mixture of the red of an invader and the blue of a friendly.

00:04:42.400 --> 00:04:45.929
If you're trying to do this with a friend or a group, I recommend setting a password.

00:04:46.900 --> 00:04:49.409
Oh, and also, if you have the Hunter's Rune memorized,

00:04:49.780 --> 00:04:54.600
according to the Guidebook, there is a 5% chance that you'll be matched with an enemy

00:04:54.600 --> 00:04:57.490
when you use your Small Resonant Bell.

00:04:57.490 --> 00:05:01.900
Speaking of the Hunter's Rune, its design actually has a lot behind it.

00:05:01.900 --> 00:05:06.660
Firstly, it's almost definitely a reference to the Brand of Sacrifice from the Berserk manga,

00:05:06.880 --> 00:05:11.429
Upon which a lot of Souls themes are based. The famous example is Artorias.

00:05:11.590 --> 00:05:14.600
There's also the wheel skeletons featured in the manga.

00:05:14.600 --> 00:05:18.390
You should totally read it, by the way. Chapter 340 was just released,

00:05:18.390 --> 00:05:21.800
so... you've got a lot of catching up to do, but it's worth it.

00:05:21.800 --> 00:05:26.340
Anyway, the shape of the mark always interested me too. It looks like a human hanging upside down,

00:05:26.410 --> 00:05:29.000
and I think that's what it just might be.

00:05:29.500 --> 00:05:35.789
The hunter's mark description describes it as a dangling, upside-down Rune, which is what clued me into it.

00:05:35.790 --> 00:05:39.332
And there are such people hung like this in the Chalice Dungeons,

00:05:39.332 --> 00:05:42.929
with their legs and hands bound together in the symbol of the Rune.

00:05:43.140 --> 00:05:46.379
I also remember learning about this being a method of torture,

00:05:46.720 --> 00:05:51.090
where all the blood runs to your head and you can lose consciousness or die.

00:05:51.090 --> 00:05:56.600
If you cut their throat, I imagine it's a good method of draining someone for blood as well.

00:05:56.600 --> 00:05:58.769
This makes the next point even more salient.

00:05:58.810 --> 00:06:02.860
Did you know that the Hunter's Mark also spells the word 'blood'?

00:06:02.860 --> 00:06:07.640
Reddit user greycross first noticed this about six months ago, and it checks out.

00:06:07.640 --> 00:06:10.890
In most games you'd probably chalk this up to a coincidence,

00:06:10.900 --> 00:06:14.500
but it's crazy how much detail From can put in sometimes.

00:06:14.500 --> 00:06:18.329
A tiny detail I noticed a while ago was to do with the pebbles.

00:06:18.490 --> 00:06:23.920
They look suspiciously like eyeballs, don't they? I was looking at one after I looted it from a crow,

00:06:23.920 --> 00:06:25.530
and I was thinking, "Hang on,

00:06:25.720 --> 00:06:28.000
Why are crows dropping pebbles?"

00:06:28.000 --> 00:06:35.000
And then it clicked: carrion crows eat eyes, crows drop pebbles, pebbles look like eyes; my God.

00:06:35.400 --> 00:06:36.899
To make this point a bit more interesting,

00:06:36.940 --> 00:06:40.500
did you know that there's a crow in Hemwick who is entirely non-hostile?

00:06:40.900 --> 00:06:43.989
His placement is in the middle of all these other crows that you're likely

00:06:44.090 --> 00:06:47.600
aggro when you try to kill them, so it's just as likely that you

00:06:47.600 --> 00:06:50.800
killed the friendly crow when you weren't paying attention.

00:06:50.800 --> 00:06:53.889
This poor innocent crow, it's all about the little things.

00:06:54.500 --> 00:06:59.980
Speaking of which always read book titles in Souls games. There's usually an Easter Egg or two.

00:06:59.980 --> 00:07:05.859
In Gherman's workshop, there's a book titled, "How to Pick Up Fair Maidens". Not much use to you here, Gherman.

00:07:06.439 --> 00:07:13.200
Another hidden thing is illusory walls, and you'd be forgiven if you didn't even think these existed in Bloodborne.

00:07:13.600 --> 00:07:18.789
Turns out they're only located in Chalice Dungeons. None have been found in the main game, though

00:07:18.789 --> 00:07:21.406
we should look out for some in the DLC, shouldn't we?

00:07:21.406 --> 00:07:25.059
There are four in the lower Pthumeru Chalice Dungeon one for each floor,

00:07:25.310 --> 00:07:29.769
but they're also known to appear randomly in (Root)? Chalice dungeons as well.

00:07:30.379 --> 00:07:33.938
Number ten is to do with the silver beasts in the Nightmare of Mensis.

00:07:34.009 --> 00:07:36.489
Did you know that they spawned three maggots upon death?

00:07:36.560 --> 00:07:41.229
You probably did know that. I didn't. I went through this area with a fire-buffed weapon.

00:07:41.229 --> 00:07:46.389
And it turns out that if you kill them with fire or a Visceral attack, then the maggots burn up inside,

00:07:46.389 --> 00:07:50.829
and they won't spawn upon death. It's a pretty useful tip if you're having some trouble.

00:07:51.589 --> 00:07:54.759
Number eleven is regarding the Forbidden Forest Gatekeeper.

00:07:55.159 --> 00:08:03.039
Willem kept two loyal servants back at Byrgenwerth. When they were sent into the labyrinth, they encountered the Eldritch Truth, and went mad.

00:08:03.379 --> 00:08:06.519
One became the Password Gatekeeper, while Dores

00:08:06.740 --> 00:08:10.329
became a grave guard of the forest. Even in madness though,

00:08:10.370 --> 00:08:15.189
They remained loyal. Keep talking to him, and eventually he'll say this:

00:08:16.189 --> 00:08:18.189
"The password...

00:08:26.000 --> 00:08:27.500
Got to close the...

00:08:43.600 --> 00:08:49.380
It's as if he's feverishly reminding himself, even in his madness, that that door has to remain closed,

00:08:49.600 --> 00:08:53.399
else people will discover the Eldritch Truth hidden at Byrgenwerth.

00:08:53.949 --> 00:08:59.759
Number twelve. We've talked before about how lore can be lost and found in translation,

00:08:59.759 --> 00:09:04.020
and Bloodborne is no exception, apparently.

00:09:04.020 --> 00:09:07.769
According to a post on the Fextralife Wiki, the original Japanese name of the Bloodletting Beast is

00:09:08.170 --> 00:09:14.670
"Host of the beast blood", which is truly interesting. I feel like we missed out on a fairly important point of the lore here.

00:09:14.700 --> 00:09:17.339
It could imply that the blood of this creature

00:09:17.860 --> 00:09:22.734
started it all, and it also makes you wonder, is there such a thing as beast blood,

00:09:22.734 --> 00:09:26.500
that's different from the blood other people are infected with?

00:09:26.500 --> 00:09:32.200
The people of Byrgenwerth, for example, near Rom, they've all turned into insect-like creatures,

00:09:32.200 --> 00:09:35.600
and the ones near Ebrietas are alien-like.

00:09:35.600 --> 00:09:38.800
So how many strains of the old blood are there?

00:09:38.800 --> 00:09:39.569
Number thirteen.

00:09:39.790 --> 00:09:45.200
Did you know that Miyazaki has confirmed the skull in the Grand Cathedral to be Lawrence?

00:09:45.200 --> 00:09:51.269
In the official strategy guide, he says that Lawrence's skull served as the start of the Healing Church itself.

00:09:51.519 --> 00:09:54.089
But it's taken the form of a twisted beast.

00:09:54.430 --> 00:10:00.510
It's interesting that he says that the skull itself served as the start of the Healing Church and not Lawrence.

00:10:00.910 --> 00:10:04.600
Maybe Lawrence became the headless Bloodletting Beast.

00:10:04.600 --> 00:10:08.279
We did just mention that he was the host of the beast blood, after all.

00:10:09.069 --> 00:10:14.909
Fourteen has to do with the Witch of Hemwick, one of the best fights that you can use low Insight to your advantage.

00:10:15.430 --> 00:10:19.344
She spawns these mad ones endlessly the first time you fight her,

00:10:19.344 --> 00:10:23.740
because you'll always have at least one Insight from initiating the fight.

00:10:23.740 --> 00:10:27.930
But if you want an easy fight, just go in there with no Insight at all,

00:10:28.029 --> 00:10:30.000
and no mad ones will spawn.

00:10:30.000 --> 00:10:31.300
It makes it a complete cakewalk.

00:10:32.000 --> 00:10:37.160
And lastly, the Hunter's Dream music changes if you acquire more than 40 insight.

00:10:37.160 --> 00:10:38.339
It changes from this:

00:10:47.870 --> 00:10:48.800
to this:

00:10:57.000 --> 00:10:58.100
Thank you all for watching.

00:10:58.100 --> 00:11:03.129
I hope you don't mind, I felt like doing a slightly easier-to-make-video after the last one,

00:11:03.290 --> 00:11:05.469
which was a much more ambitious project.

00:11:05.510 --> 00:11:10.239
I'd really appreciate if you checked it out, by the way. It's about the artists of the Souls community,

00:11:10.240 --> 00:11:14.000
and it's one of the videos I'm more proud of.

00:11:14.000 --> 00:11:18.892
I'm never really happy with a lot of the videos I put out, but I'm pretty happy with that one!

00:11:18.892 --> 00:11:20.140
Cheers guys. I'll see you in the next one.

